      <article id="policy-en" lang="en">
        <p class="intro">Tatisaki Labs (“we”, “our”, or “us”) respects your privacy. This Privacy Policy explains how Overtime Tracker BD (“the App”) collects, uses, stores, and protects information when you use the App.</p>

        <section>
          <h2>1. Information We Collect</h2>
          <p>Depending on the features you use and whether you sign in, the App may process the following information:</p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Account information:</strong> Google account name, email address, profile image (if provided by Google), and Firebase user identifier (UID) when you sign in.</li>
            <li><strong>Work and profile information:</strong> worker name, workplace or company name, designation, grade, worker/card ID, and related profile settings that you choose to enter.</li>
            <li><strong>Salary and attendance information:</strong> basic or gross salary, allowances, overtime rate, attendance and absence information, shift, overtime hours, monthly overtime target, attendance-bonus settings, night or tiffin bill details, and related notes.</li>
            <li><strong>Piece-rate information:</strong> work or item name, quantity produced, rate, date, notes, and calculated piece-rate amounts.</li>
            <li><strong>Other calculation records:</strong> advance payments, Apon Bazar deductions, calculated earnings, deductions, totals, and saved or deleted records kept in the App’s record or trash features.</li>
            <li><strong>App preferences and consent records:</strong> language or other saved preferences, Privacy Policy acceptance status, acceptance time, policy version, app version recorded in consent audit logs, and related consent audit information.</li>
            <li><strong>Notification information:</strong> Firebase Cloud Messaging may generate and process an app-specific registration token to support push notification delivery.</li>
            <li><strong>App integrity, update-check, and technical diagnostics:</strong> When you connect to the internet and use Firebase Authentication, Cloud Firestore, Firebase App Check, Google Play Integrity, or in-app update checks, Google/Firebase services may automatically process technical connection data (such as IP address, network availability status, app version, device/OS metadata, integrity attestation signals, and service diagnostics) to deliver, secure, and verify the App.</li>
            <li><strong>Advertising-related information:</strong> When Google Mobile Ads SDK (AdMob) is used to request and display ads, Google may automatically collect or share certain information, which may include the device’s IP address (which may be used to estimate general location), ad and app interactions (such as app launches, taps, and ad views), diagnostic information about app or SDK performance, and device or account identifiers (such as the Android Advertising ID, App Set ID, and, where applicable, other identifiers). The exact information processed may depend on device settings, SDK configuration, and the advertising features used.</li>
            <li><strong>Support and communication information (WhatsApp &amp; Email):</strong> The App does not automatically collect your phone number or contacts. However, if you voluntarily use the in-app “Get Direct WhatsApp Support” option or email us for help, we may receive your phone number, WhatsApp profile name/photo, email address, and the messages or details you choose to share solely to respond to your support request.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>We do not use your work records, salary details, worker ID, or profile information as ad-targeting data, and we do not intentionally send those records to AdMob for advertising personalization. We do not ask you to provide information that is unrelated to the App’s work-record and calculation features.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>2. How We Use Information</h2>
          <p>Information is used to provide and maintain the App’s features, including:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>recording attendance, overtime, and piece-rate work;</li>
            <li>calculating salary, overtime earnings, attendance bonuses, and deductions;</li>
            <li>displaying monthly summaries and generating digital pay slips;</li>
            <li>synchronizing your records across supported devices when you sign in and cloud synchronization is available;</li>
            <li>delivering relevant app notifications and service announcements;</li>
            <li>requesting and displaying banner advertisements through Google AdMob to support the free operation and maintenance of the App; Google may also use advertising-related information for ad delivery, measurement, security, and fraud prevention;</li>
            <li>protecting the App, verifying app integrity, checking for app updates, troubleshooting issues, and responding to support or account-deletion requests.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>Where personalized advertising is available, it is subject to applicable consent requirements, Google’s policies, and the user’s available device or advertising settings. If personalized advertising is not permitted or an applicable consent signal is unavailable, Google may serve non-personalized, limited, or other eligible ads instead, where supported.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>3. Local Storage and Cloud Synchronization</h2>
          <p>The App uses a local Room database on your device to store app records and preferences. This allows supported features to work locally, including when an internet connection is unavailable.</p>
          <p>When you sign in with Google, the App uses Firebase services to authenticate your account and synchronize supported records with Cloud Firestore. Cloud synchronization requires an internet connection. Data that has not successfully synchronized may remain only on your device.</p>
          <div class="note"><strong>Important:</strong> Local storage and Firebase cloud synchronization are separate. Please ensure you have an active internet connection so cloud synchronization can complete before changing devices, clearing app data, or signing out.</div>
          <p><strong>Signing out:</strong> Signing out requires an active internet connection so the App can verify and synchronize your latest records with your Firebase cloud account before clearing the App’s local database from the current device. Signing out offline is blocked to protect unsynchronized local records from loss. Signing out clears local device data only and does not delete records stored in your Firebase cloud account.</p>
          <p><strong>Android system backup:</strong> The App allows Android system backup and device-transfer features. Depending on your Android version, device settings, and backup configuration, the App’s database and selected preferences may be included in an Android backup or transferred to another device. This is an Android operating-system feature and is separate from Firebase cloud synchronization.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>4. Third-Party Services</h2>
          <p>The App uses Google and Firebase services to support core functionality and advertising. Depending on the feature, these may include:</p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Google Sign-In / Firebase Authentication</strong> for account authentication;</li>
            <li><strong>Firebase Cloud Firestore</strong> for cloud storage, synchronization, and app update checks;</li>
            <li><strong>Firebase Cloud Messaging (FCM)</strong> for push notifications;</li>
            <li><strong>Firebase App Check and Google Play Integrity</strong> to help verify that requests come from an authentic app environment;</li>
            <li><strong>Google AdMob (Google Mobile Ads SDK)</strong> to request and display banner advertisements. The SDK and Google may process advertising-related information as described in this Policy and under Google’s own terms, privacy policy, and advertising policies.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>These providers process information under their own terms and privacy policies. If you voluntarily choose to contact support via the in-app WhatsApp link, WhatsApp processes your phone number, profile details, and messages under WhatsApp’s own terms and privacy policy. We do not sell your personal information to third parties.</p>
          <p>For more information, please review <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google’s Privacy Policy</a>, <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/ads" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Advertising Technologies</a>, <a href="https://support.google.com/admob/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google AdMob Help</a>, and <a href="https://firebase.google.com/support/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Firebase Privacy and Security information</a>.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>5. Notifications</h2>
          <p>The App may provide local reminders and push notifications, such as work-record reminders and important service announcements. Local reminders are scheduled on your device. Push notifications are delivered using Firebase Cloud Messaging and may depend on your device settings, network connection, and notification permissions.</p>
          <p>You can manage notification permissions through your device settings. Disabling notifications may prevent you from receiving reminders or announcements.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>6. PDF Pay Slips and Exported Files</h2>
          <p>If you use the pay-slip feature, the App can generate a PDF file and save it to your device’s Downloads folder. The exported file is stored by Android outside the App’s local database. If you choose to share a pay slip using the App’s Share option, Android sends the selected PDF file only to the external app or recipient you choose.</p>
          <p>PDF files already saved to Downloads are not automatically deleted when you sign out or use the App’s record-deletion feature. You are responsible for deleting exported files from your device when you no longer need them.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>7. Data Sharing and Disclosure</h2>
          <p>We do not sell, rent, or trade your personal information. Information may be processed or disclosed only as reasonably necessary to:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>provide the Google, Firebase, and Google AdMob services described in this Policy, including the processing or sharing of advertising-related information by Google for ad delivery, measurement, security, and fraud prevention;</li>
            <li>protect the security, integrity, and availability of the App;</li>
            <li>comply with applicable law, legal process, or a valid request from a competent authority; or</li>
            <li>investigate suspected fraud, misuse, or security incidents.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>Your work and salary records are intended for your personal use within the App. They are not intentionally provided to AdMob for advertising personalization. Do not share your Google account or device access with anyone you do not trust.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>8. Data Retention and Deletion</h2>
          <p>Local records remain on your device until you delete them, clear the App’s data, uninstall the App, or otherwise remove them through your device. Cloud records remain associated with your Firebase account until deleted through the App where supported or through a verified account-deletion request.</p>
          <p><strong>Trash Records Retention:</strong> Records moved to the App’s Trash are kept temporarily for up to 24 hours. After 24 hours, the App automatically and permanently deletes the trashed records from the device’s local storage and, where cloud synchronization applies, the associated Cloud Firestore trash records. Once permanently deleted, these records can no longer be restored through the App.</p>
          <p><strong>Deleting records in the App:</strong> The record-deletion feature removes supported local records and attempts to remove the associated cloud records. This action is not the same as deleting your Firebase Authentication account. Some account-related consent information may remain until the account-deletion process is completed.</p>
          <p><strong>Account &amp; Data Deletion Request:</strong> You can request the deletion of your Overtime Tracker BD account and associated personal data using either of the following methods:</p>
          <p><strong>Option 1 – Website:</strong> Visit our <a href="https://mahmudappsofficial-072.github.io/overtime-tracker-bd-account-deletion/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Account &amp; Data Deletion</a> page and follow the instructions to submit your deletion request.</p>
          <p><strong>Option 2 – Email:</strong> Send an account and data deletion request to <a href="mailto:supporttatisakilabs@gmail.com?subject=Overtime%20Tracker%20BD%20-%20Account%20%26%20Data%20Deletion%20Request">supporttatisakilabs@gmail.com</a> using the email address associated with your App account. Please use “Account &amp; Data Deletion Request” as the email subject. We may ask for reasonable information to verify that you own the account.</p>
          <p>After successful verification, we manually process the request and aim to delete the Firebase Authentication account and associated cloud data within <strong>7 business days</strong>. If we need additional information to verify the request, processing time may be extended until verification is complete.</p>
          <p>Account deletion does not automatically remove PDF files previously exported to your device’s Downloads folder or copies retained independently by Android system backup. You may need to delete those files or manage your device backup separately.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>9. Data Security</h2>
          <p>We use reasonable technical and organizational measures intended to protect information, including Firebase authentication, access controls, and app-integrity checks. However, no method of electronic storage or transmission is completely secure. You are responsible for keeping your Google account and device secure.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>10. Children’s Privacy</h2>
          <p>The App is designed for people who need to record work attendance, overtime, and related earnings. It is not directed to children. We do not knowingly collect personal information from children. If you believe a child has provided personal information through the App, please contact us so that we can review the matter.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>11. Changes to This Privacy Policy</h2>
          <p>We may update this Privacy Policy when the App’s features, services, or legal requirements change. The revised version will be published on this page with an updated “Last updated” date. Please review this page periodically. Where required, we will request renewed consent through the App.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>12. Contact Us</h2>
          <p>If you have questions, privacy concerns, support inquiries, or an account-deletion request, contact:</p>
          <p><strong>Tatisaki Labs</strong><br>
          App: Overtime Tracker BD<br>
          Email: <a href="mailto:supporttatisakilabs@gmail.com">supporttatisakilabs@gmail.com</a><br>
